Subject: [Rsiena-help] help with composition change file
In-Reply-To: <34EE88C3F8566A428F1C69BBA50EFC0A03231154@icexch-m5.ic.ac.uk>
References: <34EE88C3F8566A428F1C69BBA50EFC0A03231154@icexch-m5.ic.ac.uk>
Message-ID: <4EDEA2C8.5020402@stats.ox.ac.uk>

Dear Anne,

You need to use the function sienaCompositionChangefromFile to read your 
composition change data in. The alternative list format is rather 
difficult to produce. as.list() on a data frame creates a list of 
columns not rows.

Regards,

Ruth

